   "source": [
    "# Vanity Contract Address Generator\\n",
    "\\n",
    "This notebook allows you to run the vanity contract address generator in Google Colab.\\n",
    "\\n",
    "## Instructions\\n",
    "\\n",
    "1.  **Run the setup cells:** Execute the cells under the \\"Setup\\" section to clone the repository and install the necessary Python and Node.js dependencies.\\n",
    "2.  **Modify the execution command:** In the cell under \\"Run the Application\\", replace `'YOUR_OWNER_ADDRESS'` with your actual owner address. You can also customize the `--start` and `-w` arguments to your liking. \\n",
    "    - `owner`: The owner of the vanity contract.\\n",
    "    - `--start`: The string to search for at the start of the address.\\n",
    "    - `--end`: The string to search for at the end of the address.\\n",
    "    - `-w`: The workchain of the address.\\n",
    "3.  **Run the application:** Execute the cell to start the address generation process."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Setup\\n",
    "\\n",
    "Run the following cells to clone the repository and install the necessary dependencies."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!git clone https://github.com/tonwhales/vanity-contract.git"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%cd vanity-contract"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!pip install -r requirements.txt"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!npm install -g yarn && yarn"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Run the Application\\n",
    "\\n",
    "Modify the following command with your desired arguments."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!python src/generator/run.py 'YOUR_OWNER_ADDRESS' --start 'abc' -w 0"
   ]
  }
